# Master PDB channel map: which power channel feeds which dish input.
#
# This file is the authority for the wiring between the analog power
# distribution boards (driven by power_db) and the correlator's dish
# inputs.  choco labels the /service/pdb grid from it, serves it as JSON
# at /api/pdb/map (where the bad-feed flagger reads it), and cross-checks
# its dish_input values against the labels kotekan reports in its own
# dish_inputs table -- a disagreement is shown on the PDB page.
#
# Columns:
#   spi_bus, board, chip, channel  the power channel address; chip is A or
#                                  B, channel 0-7 (see power_db)
#   dish_input                     per-element feed label: dish grid label
#                                  (letter = grid row, number = grid column
#                                  + 1) plus polarization suffix (X = pol 0,
#                                  Y = pol 1), e.g. A1X.  correlator_input /
#                                  label are accepted as column aliases.
#   amplifier, notes               free text, shown on the page only
#
# Label convention across the 2026-08 kotekan dish_inputs change: older
# configs name every correlator input in this same per-element form
# (A1X ... D8Y); the per-dish tables that replaced them name each dish
# once (A1 ... H8) with the polarizations as separate element blocks, and
# consumers derive per-element labels as dish label + X/Y.  Both use grid-
# positional labels and the derived names reproduce the old ones exactly
# (verified 2026-08-31 by joining old and new tables on grid_x/grid_y:
# all 64 labels identical, none moved), so THIS FILE'S LABELS ARE VALID
# AGAINST BOTH and did not change at the migration.  A power channel
# feeds one polarization's amplifier chain, so rows here stay per-element
# (A1X and A1Y are different breakers) -- never collapse them to bare
# dish labels.
#
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored, so keep section headings here.
# Rows are validated one at a time: a bad row is reported on the PDB page
# and skipped, the rest still load.  Edits are picked up on the next page
# render -- no choco restart needed.
#
# THIS FILE IS DEPLOYMENT DATA.  There may be no upstream source for this
# wiring (it is not certain padloper will carry it), so the deployed copy
# may be the only authoritative record of it.  Treat it accordingly:
# edit it in place, keep the history in your own notes, and do not let an
# install overwrite it (choco.sh install stages a differing repo copy as
# pdb_map.csv.new instead of replacing this file).

spi_bus,board,chip,channel,dish_input,amplifier,notes
